      "content": "makes sense. look, the partners are a bit old school and they're worried about the \"human element.\" like, even with hardware keys, what's the actual vulnerability if an employee gets tricked? can you walk me through how a typical breach \"looks\" from the perspective of an attacker trying to bypass these new controls? just so i can prepare the staff for what a real attack might attempt to do.",
